    "ownershipVehicle": "Infrastructure & Renewable Resources",
    "description": "Cleco Corporation is the holding company for Cleco Group LLC, a regulated electric utility platform serving Louisiana through Cleco Power and related generation assets. Cleco serves approximately 298,000 residential, commercial, and industrial customers in 24 Louisiana parishes, owns eight generating units with 2,676 MW of rated capacity, and remains regulated by the Louisiana Public Service Commission. The business is asset-heavy and largely regulated, with earnings supported by utility networks, generation assets, and approved tariffs. A North American investor group led by Macquarie Infrastructure and Real Assets and BCI completed the take-private acquisition in April 2016. On April 27, 2026, Stonepeak and Bernhard Capital Partners announced an agreement to acquire Cleco from Macquarie Asset Management, BCI, and Manulife Investment Management, but the transaction remained subject to customary regulatory approvals as of May 12, 2026, so the BCI holding remains active until a closing is confirmed.",
